# Copy to `.env` and fill in your own values. `.env` is git-ignored and is never
# committed. The server and the npm scripts that talk to NCBI read it when
# launched with `--env-file-if-exists=.env`; `npm start`, `dev`, `doctor`,
# `verify`, `test:live`, `verify:evals`, and `call` pass that flag.
#
# NCBI asks automated clients to identify themselves, and an API key raises the
# rate limit from 3 to 10 requests per second. Get a key from the Settings page
# of your NCBI account (https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/account/), then register
# the email and tool name by mail to eutilities@ncbi.nlm.nih.gov.

# NCBI_API_KEY=
# NCBI_EMAIL=you@example.com
# NCBI_TOOL=eutils-mcp-server
